ID: vr-71
Title: Fifteen autonomous idle face and head actions
GitHub: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/70

Status: DONE
Milestone: Tool-owned idle life without session decisions
Dependencies: vr-58, vr-65, vr-66, vr-70

Purpose:
  Make every retained head feel less static through fifteen distinct occasional
  silent actions. Verona, not a chat, chooses and times them locally.

Tasks:
  Research primary behavioral and browser scheduling sources before implementation.
  Author fifteen bounded facial/head gestures, including a stylized sneeze.
  Reuse the shared renderer and single RAF; sleep between gestures.
  Interrupt for speech, generation, media inspection and direct control use.
  Respect visibility, reduced motion, graphics loss and explicit user choice.
  Qualify all six real model paths, four presentations and selected-only resources.
  Preserve the stable live head during isolated work and save fresh settings
    before replacing only this chat's owned head.
  Update the README, engineering chapter/index, research, journal and tracking.

Acceptance criteria:
  Fifteen distinguishable action trajectories are reachable without network,
    model inference, chat prompts, new model assets or per-frame mesh rebuilding.
  One bounded local timer waits between actions; no idle RAF while waiting.
  No action overlaps generation, manual paused inspection or active playback.
    Released agent output returns to neutral without deleting its retained clip.
  Speech and direct interaction remove the idle layer immediately.
  Hidden/lost/unloaded pages cancel work; resume waits anew, never catches up.
  Actions do not overwrite voice, expression, pose, crop, colors or audio time.
  All supported native models/presentations render the shared bounded layer.
  Real qualification and visual inspection remain distinct from human accuracy
    or owner acceptance; failures remain recorded.

Completion evidence:
  Primary-source investigation and design: docs/research/idle-life.md.
  Shared implementation: verona/web/idle-life.mjs, app.js, orientation.mjs.
  Deterministic action/scheduler/lifecycle, orientation, blinking, agent-player
    and framing regressions pass; nine focused HTTP cases and JS syntax pass.
  Final actual native run idle-life-native-07 passes all six selected engines,
    four views and fifteen actions: 360 action/view cases. Zero gesture buffer
    allocations/deletions/storage/uploads/fetches; zero frames/requests in each
    0.9-second isolated wait. Real automatic selection and face/voice agent
    playback, cancellation, true-neutral release and manual inspection pass.
  All restored channels fit measured unchanged-neutral envelopes; filled
    Surface restores exactly. Wireframe baseline has 12-20 variable channels;
    no arbitrary pixel tolerance or byte-identical wireframe claim.
  Actual compact captures inspected for fifteen Claire actions and sampled
    Surface/mesh actions on five other heads. This is not human acceptance.
  Eleven qualified source/test files promoted with exact hash comparison.
    Sole owned Verona head replaced, same manager; every freshly saved old
    control/appearance restored plus enabled Idle life. No speech replay.
    Private receipt: .local/qualification/live-idle-life-01/receipt.json.
  README, prototype guide, chapter11, research, book manifest, causal ledger
    and living book/journal.md updated. Frozen PDFs/release unchanged.
  Stable lane was delivered 9b34251 until complete candidate qualification.
  Development lane: ignored detached idle-life-71 checkout, pinned model and
    Electron junction inputs, new disposable qualification outputs/profiles.
    Worktrees/junctions do not reserve CPU/GPU or enforce read-only inputs.

Completion log:
  2026-11-21 - Owner requests fifteen genuinely different occasional idle
    animations on every model, with all decisions inside the tool. Research
    precedes implementation; protect the running head and its settings.
  2026-11-21 - Keep strict readback failures01-05. Unchanged-neutral wireframe
    repeats also differ; final gate measures per-channel neutral variation.
    A nod sample between pulses is a fixture error, fixed at its first pulse.
    Correct paused agent release to use neutral buffers without deleting the
    retained clip; manually replayed voice preview takes inspection ownership.
    Final07 passes all six heads; owned live promotion at23:24:31+05:30 restores
    every saved setting and enables the tool-owned autonomous layer.
